# VoterGuard India: project rules for Cline

PURPOSE
Open-source, non-partisan toolkit that audits electoral-roll revisions using synthetic data,
flags unusual booth-level patterns for human verification, and records report hashes on a
local blockchain. It NEVER decides voter eligibility and NEVER declares fraud.

LANGUAGE SAFETY (applies to all code comments, UI text, explanations, and test data)
- Do not write: fraud, illegal, rigging, ineligible, foreigner, infiltrator, "wrongly deleted"
  as a conclusion.
- Use: unusual, worth verifying, recommend a field check, consistent with / may indicate.
- Never infer religion, caste, or citizenship from names. Only gender and age bands are analysed.

DATA
- Synthetic data only. Never scrape or hardcode real voter data. EPIC numbers start with VGX.
- Public output is aggregate by default; individual records are masked.

OWNERSHIP (never edit outside your allowed folders; message your teammate instead)
- Member A: backend/, agent-service/, contracts/, scripts/, .env.example, Makefile
- Member B: frontend/, trust-service/, chain/, docs/, README.md
- The API contract is contracts/CONTRACT.md. Follow it exactly. Do not rename fields.

ENGINEERING
- All numbers, flags and scores come from deterministic code. An LLM may only phrase text.
- Python 3.11 with type hints; Node 22 with TypeScript strict mode.
- Every module gets tests. Keep functions small and documented.
- Every service must run with a single command and expose GET /health or /api/health.
- Prefer boring, well-known libraries. No unnecessary abstractions.
- Never commit secrets, node_modules, data/, .venv, or build artifacts.